				<h1 id="versionHeadLine" class="headline">

Candidates and Measures on the Ballot		</h1>
	
		<div id="cc5f8c90dc-b4cb-431b-90ee-10648f8df655" data-containerid="5f8c90dc-b4cb-431b-90ee-10648f8df655" class="pageContent cpGrid cpGrid24"  data-contentcontainerbreakpoint="15" data-smoothscrolling="True">
			

		<div class="row outer wide"><!--
--><div class="outer col col24 first last" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="7edef63a-a138-4403-9dd3-b3e1bac3902e">				
	<div class="row nest first last wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last idb5f8efa6-2922-46f7-a165-885ffd911b0f" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="b5f8efa6-2922-46f7-a165-885ffd911b0f">	
<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor19c613a6-a520-4ea0-94b2-ef5dd7b569c1" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>Find official information about what&apos;s on your ballot for the current election, including voters&apos; guides, a sample ballot, ballot measures, resolutions received, and other important ballot information.</p><p><br></p><div style="border-left: 3px solid #E5E7EB;"><h2 style="margin: 0 0 1em 1em;"><strong>Jump to Section:</strong></h2><ul style="list-style: none;"><li style="margin:.35rem 0;"><a style="color:#344B5E;" href="#Sample-Ballot">Sample Ballot</a></li><li style="margin:.35rem 0;"><a style="color:#344B5E;" href="#Voters-Guides">Voters&apos; Guides</a></li><li style="margin:.35rem 0;"><a style="color:#344B5E;" href="/DocumentCenter/View/151457" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">View Current Voters&apos; Pamphlet PDF</a></li><li style="margin:.35rem 0;"><a style="color:#284860;" href="#Resolutions">Resolutions Submitted by Districts</a></li><li style="margin:.35rem 0;"><a style="color:#344B5E;" href="#About-Ballot-Measures">About Measures on the Ballot</a></li><li style="margin:.35rem 0;"><a style="color:#344B5E;" href="#About-Candidates">About Candidates on the Ballot</a></li></ul></div><hr style="border:1px solid black;" id="Sample-Ballot" aria-hidden="true"><h2 style="background-color:#284860; color:white; font-weight: 700; padding: 5px;margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:1em;">What&apos;s on the Ballot</h2><p>The sample ballot contains all the candidates and/or measures that will be voted on in Snohomish County. It may look different from the official ballot you receive in the mail, which has only the candidates and/or measures you are eligible to vote on.</p><ul role="presentation"><li><h3><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/128277" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message"><strong>Sample Ballot</strong> (PDF)</a></h3></li><li><h3 role="presentation" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/152257/Boleta-de-muestraprovisional-para-las-elecciones-oficiales-generales-3-de-noviembre-de-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Boleta de muestra (PDF)</a></h3></li></ul><hr style="border:1px solid black;" id="Voters-Guides" aria-hidden="true"><h2 style="background-color:#284860; color:white; font-weight: 700; padding: 5px;margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:1em;">Finding Information on Candidates and Measures</h2><p>Your voters&rsquo; guide is the best place to get information on the candidates and measures that appear on your ballot. The voters&rsquo; guide lets candidates tell you who they are and what they stand for. Explanations of bond and levy measures, as well as statements for and against each measure, are also included in the voters&apos; guide.<br><br>The voters&apos; guide is available in two formats:</p><ul style="margin-bottom:0px;"><li><h3><a href="https://voter.votewa.gov/WhereToVote.aspx" class="external_link"><strong>Online Voters&rsquo; Guide (VoteWA)</strong></a></h3>Contains only the candidates and issues on your ballot. Once you log in, click on the &quot;Voters&rsquo; Guide&quot; tab on the left of your screen.&nbsp;<br><br></li><li><h3><strong>Local Voters&apos; Pamphlet</strong></h3>Includes information on candidates and/or measures that will be voted on in Snohomish County. Every household is mailed one Local Voters&apos; Pamphlet in primary and general elections. It is mailed either as an insert with the ballot or separately to households for special elections.<br><br><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/151457"><strong>View the</strong><strong>&nbsp;Local Voters&apos; Pamphlet (PDF)</strong></a><br><br><a href="/DocumentCenter/View/152029/Folleto_Electoral_de_Snohomish_Elecciones_Elecciones-Generales-3-de-noviembre"><strong>Consulte el folleto de las elecciones generales del 3 de noviembre (PDF)</strong></a><br><br></li><li><h3><a href="https://lwvsnoho.org/content.aspx?page_id=22&club_id=108940&module_id=563630" class="external_link"><strong>League of Women Voters&apos; Candidate Forums</strong></a></h3>These nonpartisan candidate forums, hosted by the <a href="https://lwvsnoho.org/">Snohomish County League of Women Voters</a>, provide an opportunity for voters to hear directly from candidates in contested races as they respond to questions from a moderator. Voters can tune in for the live streams or view the recordings.</li></ul>
    </div>

