	<div class="row nest first last wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last id10c1e5d2-abda-49fb-b668-9ebac969bb8c" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="10c1e5d2-abda-49fb-b668-9ebac969bb8c">	
<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor5198d45d-6e51-49c5-960b-b1c311a9be55" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <h3 style="margin-bottom: 0px;">Common questions about ballot measures (click or tap to expand):</h3>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + '5198d45d-6e51-49c5-960b-b1c311a9be55'));
	});
</script>
</div>

	</div> <!-- inner column -->

	</div> <!-- inner row -->

			</div><!-- outer column --><!--		--></div> <!-- outer row -->
		<div class="row outer wide"><!--
--><div class="outer col col24 first last" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="e62931f0-8013-4de7-9f6e-237c650be3d2">				
	<div class="row nest first last wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last id1039ae2f-41c3-417a-bfce-1422d9dcea97" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="1039ae2f-41c3-417a-bfce-1422d9dcea97">	

	<div id="divTabbed4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829" class="widget widgetTabbed narrow skin105 accordionTabs" data-widgetid="4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829">

		<div class="cpTabPanels">
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_0" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_0" role="button" aria-controls="tab4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_0" aria-expanded="false" ><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="0" data-tabname="What are ballot measures?" contenteditable="false">What are ballot measures?</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_0" role="region" aria-labelledby="tabBtn4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_0" >

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditorea367e4c-f617-424e-bcd5-aeee40424ad6" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>A ballot measure is a question that voters are asked to approve or reject in an election. Local districts use ballot measures to make decisions or raise funding for services and projects. A short summary for each measure is included on the ballot, and the full details are provided in the voters&apos; pamphlet. There are different types of measures:<br><br></p><ul><li><strong>Levy:&nbsp;</strong>Usually provides funding for ongoing local services like schools, fire protection, emergency medical services, hospitals, libraries, and more. School levies only need a simple majority of &quot;yes&quot; votes, while others require a 60% supermajority. Levy measures expire after a set number of years, and voter approval is required to renew the levy.<br><br></li><li><strong>Bond:</strong> Allows a district to borrow funds for major capital projects, like building schools or public facilities. Funds are repaid over time through property taxes. Bonds always require a 60% supermajority and a minimum voter turnout.&nbsp;<br><br></li><li><strong>Other measures:</strong> Can include sales taxes, levy lid lifts, and non-revenue measures that require voter approval.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>Some measures are placed on the ballot through petition initiatives or referenda. Learn more about how these work on our <a href="https://www.snohomishcountywa.gov/5736/Petitions-for-Initiatives-and-Referenda">Petitions for Initiatives and Referenda</a> page.</p>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + 'ea367e4c-f617-424e-bcd5-aeee40424ad6'));
	});
</script>
</div>

				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_1" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_1" role="button" aria-controls="tab4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_1" aria-expanded="false" ><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="1" data-tabname="How are ballot measures passed?" contenteditable="false">How are ballot measures passed?</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_1" role="region" aria-labelledby="tabBtn4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_1" >

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditorfa25d556-639b-480c-b405-04f320a7cca3" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>Not all ballot measures are approved the same way. Some only need a simple majority of more than 50% of the votes to pass, while others have a higher threshold of requirements or additional rules. Here&apos;s a breakdown:<br>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>Simple Majority Measures:</strong> Most measures, like sales taxes, school levies, and levy lid lifts, pass if more than 50% of voters vote &quot;yes.&quot; No minimum voter turnout is required.<br><br></li><li><strong>Supermajority Measures:&nbsp;</strong>Other measures require at least 60% &quot;yes&quot; votes, or a supermajority, to pass.&nbsp;<br><br></li><li><strong>Turnout Rules</strong><strong>:&nbsp;</strong>Certain measures also require a minimum number of voters to participate, based off voter turnout in the last general election:<br><br></li><li style="margin-left: 40px; list-style-type: circle;"><strong>Bonds:&nbsp;</strong>Must receive 60% &quot;yes&quot; votes <em><strong>and</strong></em><strong>&nbsp;</strong>at least 40% turnout of the voters who participated in the last general election. So, a bond measure could receive the required number of &quot;yes&quot; votes and still fail if not enough people vote in the election.<br><br></li><li style="margin-left: 40px; list-style-type: circle;"><strong>Levy ballot measure:</strong> Must receive at least 60% &ldquo;yes&rdquo; votes and meet validation requirements based on voter participation in the most recent general election. Validation is met either through sufficient voter turnout or by meeting a minimum number of &ldquo;yes&rdquo; votes set by law.<br>&nbsp;</li><li><strong>School Levies:</strong> Only a simple majority of votes cast is required.</li></ul><p>For more detailed information, see <a href="https://www.snohomishcountywa.gov/DocumentCenter/View/96/Validation-Requirements?bidId=" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.snohomishcountywa.gov/DocumentCenter/View/96/Validation-Requirements?bidId=" data-url-hash="e31df44a2ddb158d4057d434adb97c28322b5e56e295a5e7e2ca0c7839ecc188" data-url-status="disabled" class="docaccess-activated"><strong>Validation Requirements (PDF)</strong></a>.&nbsp;Specific details about the ballot measures that appear on your ballot can be found in the voters&apos; pamphlet. If you have additional questions, please reach out to the district&apos;s representative.</p>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + 'fa25d556-639b-480c-b405-04f320a7cca3'));
	});
</script>
</div>

				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_2" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_2" role="button" aria-controls="tab4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_2" aria-expanded="false" ><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="2" data-tabname="If a levy or bond passes, how will it affect my taxes and local services?" contenteditable="false">If a levy or bond passes, how will it affect my taxes and local services?</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_2" role="region" aria-labelledby="tabBtn4592dc09-8c8b-4778-88ac-40f72514e829_2" >

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor4c92ecff-e038-455e-87c5-dca904e08616" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>When a levy/bond passes, the impact on the services your community receives and the taxes you may pay depends greatly on your unique situation. For the information on proposed uses for funding measures, see your voters&rsquo; guide or reach out to your district representative. You can find your elected officials on <a href="//VoteWA.gov">VoteWA.gov</a> or by using our&nbsp;<a href="https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/0a219ac968ee4ddc833491fc7b7a7ca9/">interactive district map</a>.<br><br>For information on how your current property taxes are distributed, please visit the <a href="https://www.snohomishcountywa.gov/2934/Assessor">Snohomish County Assessor&rsquo;s website</a>.</p>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + '4c92ecff-e038-455e-87c5-dca904e08616'));
	});
</script>
</div>

				</div>
					</div>
	</div>
