		<div class="row outer wide"><!--
--><div class="outer col col24 first last" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="857950ab-8eff-4ead-95bd-b252dc22ff8f">				
	<div class="row nest first last wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last id13da26e1-03b3-43f1-99e8-22d52b2eb91e" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="13da26e1-03b3-43f1-99e8-22d52b2eb91e">	
<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor99cea8d2-22fc-400a-9633-79c87e9906b6" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <hr style="border:1px solid black;" id="About-Candidates" aria-hidden="true"><h2 style="background-color:#284860; color:white; font-weight: 700; padding: 5px;margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:1em;">Candidates on the Ballot</h2><p>Candidate filing takes place during the first full week of May. This is when individuals officially submit their paperwork to run for federal, state, or local office.<br><br>After candidate filing closes, a primary election is held in August to narrow the field of candidates before the General Election in November.&nbsp;<br><br><strong data-pasted="true">Nonpartisan&nbsp;</strong><strong>offices:&nbsp;</strong>Candidates appear on the primary ballot only if more than two people filed for the position. If two or fewer candidates filed for the position, they advance directly to the General Election.<br><br><strong>Partisan offices:&nbsp;</strong>Candidates running for partisan offices always appear on the primary ballot, even if only one or two candidates filed for the position. A partisan office is a government position in which candidates may specify a political party preference, but their stated preference does not mean the party endorses or approves the candidate.&nbsp;<br><br></p><p>To view the offices that affect your area, enter your address in our&nbsp;<a href="https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/0a219ac968ee4ddc833491fc7b7a7ca9/">Find Your District and Elected Officials interactive map</a>.<br><br></p><h3>Common questions about candidates on the ballot (click or tap to expand):</h3>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + '99cea8d2-22fc-400a-9633-79c87e9906b6'));
	});
</script>
</div>

	</div> <!-- inner column -->

	</div> <!-- inner row -->

			</div><!-- outer column --><!--		--></div> <!-- outer row -->
		<div class="row outer wide"><!--
--><div class="outer col col24 first last" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="42b896a8-03ba-401c-9f33-a69c6f07fc9b">				
	<div class="row nest first last wide">
	
	<div class="inner col col24 first last ide0e31edb-4627-49e5-8958-592793a56297" style="" data-widgetcontainerid="e0e31edb-4627-49e5-8958-592793a56297">	

	<div id="divTabbed1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c" class="widget widgetTabbed narrow skin105 accordionTabs" data-widgetid="1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c">

		<div class="cpTabPanels">
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_0" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_0" role="button" aria-controls="tab1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_0" aria-expanded="false" ><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="0" data-tabname="Why don&#39;t I see a particular candidate on my ballot?" contenteditable="false">Why don't I see a particular candidate on my ballot?</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_0" role="region" aria-labelledby="tabBtn1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_0" >

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor1bb22c94-bedb-4c33-bfad-7ac0d19908b0" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>We use your residential address to determine the candidates and measures that appear on your ballot. You can check your local, state, and federal districts and elected officials using our&nbsp;<a href="https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/0a219ac968ee4ddc833491fc7b7a7ca9/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message" class="external_link">interactive district map</a>.<br><br>In a primary election, candidates who have filed for a <strong>partisan position</strong> will always appear on the primary ballot, regardless of how many people filed to run for that position. Candidates who have filed for a&nbsp;<strong>nonpartisan position&nbsp;</strong>appear on the primary ballot only if more than two candidates filed for that position. Otherwise, they will advance directly to the general election in November.<br><br></p>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + '1bb22c94-bedb-4c33-bfad-7ac0d19908b0'));
	});
</script>
</div>

				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_1" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_1" role="button" aria-controls="tab1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_1" aria-expanded="false" ><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="1" data-tabname="Where can I find the descriptions and responsibilities of elected offices?" contenteditable="false">Where can I find the descriptions and responsibilities of elected offices?</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_1" role="region" aria-labelledby="tabBtn1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_1" >

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditorb3ad8e88-c7e3-44c3-ab1c-ac413385a395" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>We provide descriptions of all elected positions on the ballot in the Local Voters&apos; Pamphlet for the election. You can also find qualifications and responsibilities for federal and state elected offices on the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.sos.wa.gov/elections/candidates/information/descriptions-elected-offices" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="external_link" aria-describedby="audioeye_new_window_message">Secretary of State&apos;s website</a>.&nbsp;<br><br></p>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + 'b3ad8e88-c7e3-44c3-ab1c-ac413385a395'));
	});
</script>
</div>

				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_2" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_2" role="button" aria-controls="tab1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_2" aria-expanded="false" ><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="2" data-tabname="Why aren&#39;t candidate names displayed in alphabetical order?" contenteditable="false">Why aren't candidate names displayed in alphabetical order?</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_2" role="region" aria-labelledby="tabBtn1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c_2" >

<div class="widget editor pageStyles narrow" id="divEditor62ded021-0534-4a24-bc0a-216947333afc" data-elementqueryclasses='{"wide-narrow":"min-width:25em"}'>
	    <div class="fr-view">


        <p>As required by state law, the order that candidates&apos; names appear on the ballot and in the Local Voters&apos; Pamphlet is determined by a random lot drawing, which is held by staff at the end of filing week. During this process, staff and a member of the public pull lettered tiles from a rotating &quot;bingo barrel.&quot; The order that the lettered tiles are drawn in is recorded and becomes the official candidate listing order.<br><br>The lot drawing is <a href="https://www.snohomishcountywa.gov/5731/Observe-the-Elections-Process">open to the public to observe</a>, and the final listing order is publicly available on our&nbsp;<a href="https://www.snohomishcountywa.gov/5729/Run-for-Office">Run for Office page</a>.&nbsp;<br><br></p>
    </div>

<script type="text/javascript">
	$(document).ready(function (e) {		
	    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + '62ded021-0534-4a24-bc0a-216947333afc'));
	});
</script>
</div>

				</div>
					</div>
	</div>
	<script type="text/javascript">

		//If responsive not enabled, execute this after a timeout
		if(!isResponsiveEnabled)
		{
			window.setTimeout(function(){
				var tabbedWidgetID = 'divTabbed1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c';
				typeof setTabbedWidgetsTabHeight === "function" && setTabbedWidgetsTabHeight(tabbedWidgetID);
			}, 1500);
		}

		function reinitCarousels() {
			if (window.carouselsToInit) {
				for (var i = 0; i < window.carouselsToInit.length; i++) {
					carouselsToInit[i]();
				}
			}
		}
		function sizeTabbedContent(element){
			if(window.Pages){
				if(window.Pages.onResizeHandlers){
					var setTabbedInterval = setInterval(function () {
						window.Pages.onResizeHandlers.forEach(function(car){car();});
					}, 25)


					setTimeout(function () {
						clearInterval(setTabbedInterval);
						if ($.cookie("enableLiveEdit") === "true") {
							setInterval(function () {
								window.Pages.onResizeHandlers.forEach(function(car){car();});
							}, 2000);
						}
					}, 2500);
					element.onclick="window.setTimeout(function(){reinitCarousels();},2);"
				}
			}
		}

		function adjustTab(e) {
			e.preventDefault();
			window.setTimeout(function(){
				reinitCarousels();
			}, 2);
			sizeTabbedContent(this);
		}

		var tabButtons = document.querySelectorAll("#divTabbed1af7958b-9fc9-40fa-b213-d4e45318b11c .tabButton");

		tabButtons.forEach(function (tabButton) {
			tabButton.addEventListener("click", adjustTab);
		});

	</script>



